# libcss: four corner radii; border-radius as their shorthand (patch 363, with 363-netsurf)
# Generated 2026-11-01
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 361)
#
# border-radius was one length for all four corners; any second value
# dropped the declaration as junk, and the corner longhands were unknown
# properties. The r86 scorecard census dropped corner-radius declarations
# on 17 of 21 sites (claude 83, oldreddit 56, youtube 51, github 33).
#
#  - CSS_PROP_BORDER_{TOP_LEFT,TOP_RIGHT,BOTTOM_RIGHT,BOTTOM_LEFT}_RADIUS
#    (0x0ae-0x0b1): <length-percentage>{1,2} (horizontal, vertical), not
#    inherited, initial 0. Stored beside 358's stroke fields (status, h
#    length + unit, v length + unit per corner); read with
#    css_computed_border_corner_radius(style, corner, ...). A percentage
#    is of the border box's width (h) or height (v).
#  - border-radius is now their shorthand: <lp>{1,4} [ / <lp>{1,4} ],
#    each list filled out as margin's is; inherit / initial / unset set
#    all four. css_computed_border_radius() reads the top-left corner, so
#    older callers keep working.
#  - Aliases (alias_props): -webkit-border-radius, -moz-border-radius,
#    -webkit-border-{corner}-radius, and the logical corners
#    border-{start,end}-{start,end}-radius as horizontal-tb left-to-right
#    places them. var() works through the existing deferral.
#  - Wiring as for 358: property enum, opcodes, important.c (4 operands),
#    property strings, parse/dispatch tables, Makefiles,
#    p_border_corner_radius.c, s_border_corner_radius.c.
#
# Not covered: calc() in a corner (about 6 declarations in the census;
# the declaration is still dropped), and the -moz-border-radius-topleft
# style corner names.
#
